HumanLang (the language, its interpreter, this website, the Playground, the courses, the games and everything else in
this repository) is free for everybody to USE. It is not free to COPY. Please read both parts.

1. WHAT YOU MAY DO (free, no sign-up, no payment)
   a. Use HumanLang: install it, run it, use the website and the Playground, take the courses, play the games.
   b. Write your own programs, games and pages in HumanLang and do anything you like with them: share them, publish them,
      sell them. What you create is yours. This licence puts no rule on your own programs.
   c. Read the source code in this repository to learn from it.
   d. Use GitHub's Fork button only to suggest a change to this project (a pull request). Such a fork must not be
      published as a project of its own.
   e. Quote short parts of the documentation or code, with credit and a link to this project, for review, teaching or
      news.

2. WHAT YOU MAY NOT DO without written permission from the copyright holder
   a. Copy, fork or mirror this project (all or a substantial part) to publish, host or distribute it, in source or built form.
   b. Make or publish a modified version, a derivative, a "port", a clone or a "new language" built from this code,
      its documentation, its courses, its website, its games or its design.
   c. Sell, rent, sublicense or give away copies of HumanLang or of its parts, or bundle them into another product.
   d. Host your own copy of the website, the Playground or the courses.
   e. Remove or change this licence, the copyright notice, or the credits.
   f. Use the name "HumanLang", the abbreviation "HL" for a programming language, or the HumanLang logo, mascots,
      certificate artwork or game artwork for another product, project or service, or in a way that suggests it comes from,
      or is approved by, this project.
   g. Use this project's code, text or artwork to train or build a competing programming language or learning course.

3. VERSIONS ALREADY PUBLISHED UNDER MIT
   Releases published on GitHub with tags v0.6.1 and earlier were published under the MIT License. People who already
   have those releases may keep using them under the MIT License. This licence applies to everything published after
   them (all later commits and releases), and to the name and artwork in every version.

4. CONTRIBUTIONS
   If you send a change to this project, you promise that it is yours to give, and you give the copyright holder a
   permanent, worldwide, free licence to use, change, publish and relicense it as part of HumanLang. You keep your own
   copyright in it.

5. NO WARRANTY
   HumanLang is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind. The copyright holder is not liable for any damage
   that comes from using it.

6. ENDING
   If you break section 2 your permission under this licence ends. The copyright holder may ask for any copy to be
   removed, including through GitHub's copyright (DMCA) process.

7. QUESTIONS AND PERMISSION
   Want to do something section 2 forbids (for example to teach with a copy in your school)? Ask first: open an issue
   at https://github.com/notsabbir4/HumanLang or write to the owner. Permission must be given in writing.
